# Spec: the seed module (synthetic test data)

The template manages this file, and `copier update` refreshes it. It is the contract for the `seed/` Gradle
subproject, which the template generates when `with_seed_module` is `true` in `.copier-answers.yml`. An agent
reads it before it adds or changes code under `seed/`, and when the golden test or `standTest` fails.

## 1. Intent

`seed/` builds synthetic datasets, loads them onto a stand, and shows what the load changed:

- `generate` turns a seed and a size preset into a `Scenario` with Datafaker. The same seed and preset always
  give the same files.
- `load` pushes a scenario to the stand through the services and steps of the main project.
- `diff` compares the stand state with the checkpoint that `load` recorded.

It is a client of the main project (`src/main`), not a second framework: it reuses the configs, services, steps
and verifications there and adds none of its own.

## 2. Layout

`<base>` is `<package_root>.<package_name>` from `.copier-answers.yml`. Put each class into the package of its
concern, and do not create other packages under `<base>.seed`. Every package has a `package-info.java` that states
its purpose.

```text
seed/
  build.gradle                 template-managed: `copier update` replaces it, do not edit
  gradle/dependencies.gradle   the project's: repositories and dependencies of seed/
  gradle/seed.versions.toml    the project's: version catalog `seedLibs` (Datafaker, q4j jackson-json)
  src/main/java/<base>/seed/
    scenario/    the serialized dataset contract: Scenario (versioned schema), SyntheticUser, SyntheticMarkers, SeedJson
    generate/    Datafaker with a seeded Random (FakeValues, the only Datafaker caller), SizePreset, ScenarioGenerator
    format/      builders that mirror the application's own storage formats (UserCsv)
    files/       deterministic binary fixtures such as images and PDFs (PngFixture)
    stand/       StandProbe: reads the stand state through the main project's steps and configs
    load/        ScenarioLoader: orchestration only, pushes a scenario through the main project's steps
    checkpoint/  Checkpoint (snapshot of the stand state) and CheckpointDiff
    cli/         SeedCli and one thin command class per command: generate, load, diff
  src/main/resources/META-INF/services/   registrations of the ScenarioLoader and StandProbe implementations
  src/test/java/<base>/seed/   tests, in the package of the class they test
  src/test/resources/golden/   expected output of `generate` (determinism guard)
src/main/java/<base>/config/SeedConfig.java   defaults of the command line (SEED_PRESET, SEED_DIR)
src/main/resources/seed.properties
```

## 3. Requirements

Each requirement can be checked with a file read or a command, run from the project root.

| ID  | Requirement | Check |
| --- | ----------- | ----- |
| S1  | `settings.gradle` has `include 'seed'` and declares the catalog `seedLibs` from `seed/gradle/seed.versions.toml`. | read `settings.gradle` |
| S2  | `seed/build.gradle` is the template file of the same template version. Seed dependencies go in `seed/gradle/dependencies.gradle`. | `diff` against the template's seed `build.gradle.jinja` at `<ref>`, the `_commit` of `.copier-answers.yml` |
| S3  | `seed/` depends on the main project with `implementation project(':')`. The main project has no seed source sets, and no build script adds `sourceSets.main.output` to another classpath. | `grep -rn 'sourceSets.main.output' build.gradle gradle seed/gradle` prints nothing |
| S4  | Datafaker is declared only in `seed/gradle/dependencies.gradle`, from the `seedLibs` catalog, whose `q4j` version equals the one in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`, and `generate/FakeValues` is the only class that imports `net.datafaker`. | `grep -rln 'net.datafaker' seed/src src` prints only `FakeValues.java` |
| S5  | No parallel services: `seed/` has no `*Service`, `*Steps` or `*Verification` classes, sends no requests itself and opens no database connections. Requests go through a service in `src/main/.../service` and a steps class in `src/main/.../step`; extend those, or add them there. | `grep -rnE 'RestAssured\|java\.net\.http\|java\.sql\|DriverManager' seed/src` prints nothing |
| S6  | Every setting comes from an Owner config in `<base>.config`, read through `ConfigRegistry` (AGENTS.md rule 2). No `System.getenv` or `System.getProperty` in `seed/`. | `grep -rnE 'System\.(getProperty\|getenv)' seed/src` prints nothing |
| S7  | HTTP status codes are `org.apache.http.HttpStatus` constants (AGENTS.md rule 10). | `grep -rniE 'status[a-z]*\(.*\b[1-5][0-9]{2}\b' seed/src` prints nothing |
| S8  | Pages are used only through their `*PageSteps`; `seed/` never imports a `*Page` class. | review the imports |
| S9  | Every generated identifier and contact value carries a marker of `SyntheticMarkers`, and the markers are defined only there. | review; `SyntheticMarkers.isSynthetic` is true for each id and email |
| S10 | `generate`, `format` and `files` are deterministic: no unseeded `Random`, no `UUID.randomUUID`, no clock. The golden test passes. | `./gradlew :seed:test` |
| S11 | Unit tests are named `*Test` and run in `:seed:test`, which `check` runs. Tests that change the stand are named `*StandTest` and run only in `:seed:standTest`. No TestNG groups (AGENTS.md rule 9). | `./gradlew :seed:test` prints no `*StandTest` |
| S12 | `seed/` passes `:seed:archgateCheck` with `rootPackage = '<base>.seed'` and the same rule list as the main project. | `./gradlew :seed:archgateCheck` prints `Gate PASSED` |
| S13 | CI runs `:seed:standTest` in its own job against a stand, not in the job of the end-to-end tests and never concurrently against one stand, and uploads `seed/build/allure-results` (section 7). | read the CI configuration |

Why S4 needs care: `seed/gradle/seed.versions.toml` repeats the `q4j` version of the root catalog, and the two
must stay equal. Renovate updates them in one pull request only when it groups the q4j artifacts. The shared
[quokkify/renovate-presets](https://github.com/quokkify/renovate-presets) is getting such a group; until a preset
the project extends has it, add this rule to the project's Renovate configuration:

```json
{
  "packageRules": [
    {
      "matchDatasources": ["maven"],
      "matchPackageNames": ["/^dev\\.quokkify:/"],
      "groupName": "q4j"
    }
  ]
}
```

Why `*StandTest` and not `*IT`: the `TestClassNamingRule` of the architecture gate requires every class with
`@Test` methods to end in `Test`, so a `*IT` class fails S12. The suffix `StandTest` keeps that rule and still
selects the stand tests by name.

## 4. Extension points

`load` and `diff` call two interfaces that the project implements, because only the project knows its services
and its database:

- `<base>.seed.load.ScenarioLoader`: `void load(Scenario scenario)`. Push the scenario through the steps of the
  main project.
- `<base>.seed.stand.StandProbe`: `Map<String, String> capture()`. Read the stand state that a checkpoint records,
  for example a row count per table, through the database or API steps of the main project.

Write each as a public class with a public no-argument constructor in its package (`load/`, `stand/`), and list
its fully qualified name in `seed/src/main/resources/META-INF/services/<base>.seed.load.ScenarioLoader` or
`.../<base>.seed.stand.StandProbe`. `ServiceRegistrationRule` checks both files. Register exactly one implementation of each: with none, or with
more than one, `load` and `diff` stop with a message that names the file to fix.

Unit tests never call a registered implementation, because it changes or reads the real stand. They test
`LoadCommand` and `DiffCommand` with lambdas, and `discover(ClassLoader)` with an empty class loader. A test that
needs the real implementations is a `*StandTest` (section 7).

```java
// seed/src/main/java/<base>/seed/load/ApiScenarioLoader.java
public class ApiScenarioLoader implements ScenarioLoader {
  private final UserApiSteps userApiSteps = new UserApiSteps();

  @Override
  public void load(Scenario scenario) {
    scenario.users().forEach(user -> {
      ValidatableResponse response = userApiSteps.createUser(new UserPojo(user.id(), user.fullName(), user.email()));
      userApiSteps.verify().verifyResponseStatusCode(response, HttpStatus.SC_CREATED);
    });
  }
}

// seed/src/main/java/<base>/seed/stand/DbStandProbe.java
public class DbStandProbe implements StandProbe {
  private final UserDbSteps userDbSteps = new UserDbSteps();

  @Override
  public Map<String, String> capture() {
    return Map.of("users", String.valueOf(userDbSteps.countUsers()));
  }
}
```

`UserApiSteps`, `UserPojo` and `UserDbSteps` live in `src/main`, as AGENTS.md section 2 describes. `seed/` sees the
classes of the main project, but not the libraries the main project declares as `implementation`. Declare each
q4j module whose types the code under `seed/` uses in `seed/gradle/dependencies.gradle`, from the root catalog,
for example `implementation libs.q4j.rest.assured`.

## 5. Commands

Run from the project root. A relative `--dir` resolves against `seed/`, the working directory of `run`.

```sh
./gradlew :seed:run --args='generate --seed 1'                     # SEED_PRESET into SEED_DIR (seed/build/seed)
./gradlew :seed:run --args='generate --seed 7 --preset large --dir build/large'
./gradlew :seed:run --args='load'                                  # writes checkpoint.json, then loads scenario.json
./gradlew :seed:run --args='diff'                                  # writes diff.json: changes since that checkpoint
```

`generate` writes `scenario.json`, `users.csv` and `avatars/<id>.png`. `load` and `diff` read and write in the
same directory. The presets are `small` (5 users), `medium` (100) and `large` (1000).

## 6. Determinism and the golden file

`SeedCliTest.generateMatchesTheGoldenScenario` runs `generate --seed 1 --preset small` and compares
`scenario.json` with `seed/src/test/resources/golden/scenario-seed-1-small.json`. It fails when a code change, a
package move or a Datafaker upgrade changes the generated data. Then:

1. Decide whether the change is intended. A refactoring that changes the data is a bug.
2. If the scenario contract changed so that an older file no longer reads, raise `Scenario.SCHEMA_VERSION`.
3. Replace the golden file with the file the failure message names, and say in the change description why the
   data changed.

`FakeValues` takes its values from one seeded `Random` in call order. Add a new field at the end of the
generation of a record, so that the values of the fields before it stay the same.

## 7. Tests and CI

| Task | Runs | Part of `check` |
| ---- | ---- | --------------- |
| `:seed:test` | `*Test` classes except `*StandTest`: no stand needed | yes |
| `:seed:standTest` | `*StandTest` classes: change the stand | no |

Both tasks run through the q4j TestNG extensions and write Allure results to `seed/build/allure-results`
([test-execution.md](test-execution.md), [test-reporting.md](test-reporting.md)). `standTest` succeeds when there
is no `*StandTest` class yet.

Run `standTest` in a CI job of its own, never in the same job or Gradle run as the end-to-end tests of the main
project, and never from two runs at once against the same stand. A java component in ci-kit's
`.ci/modules/java.yml` runs on every pull request and push, so it does not fit: it would change the shared stand
from parallel runs and next to the end-to-end tests. Until ci-kit can run such a component with secrets and after
other jobs ([quokkify/ci-kit#547](https://github.com/quokkify/ci-kit/issues/547)), add a workflow of the project's
own, for example `.github/workflows/seed-stand.yml`. It is not a ci-kit-rendered file, so ci-kit leaves it alone.
It calls the reusable ci-kit `java-ci.yml` on demand and on a schedule, with one `concurrency` group per stand:

```yaml
name: Seed stand tests

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
  schedule:
    - cron: "0 3 * * 1-5"

concurrency:
  group: stand-<stand name>
  cancel-in-progress: false

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  stand:
    uses: quokkify/ci-kit/.github/workflows/java-ci.yml@<the ci-kit tag of .copier-answers.core.yml>
    with:
      working-directory: test-automation
      java-version: "21"
      run-lint: false
      run-build: false
      test-command: ./gradlew :seed:standTest --console=plain
      upload-test-artifacts: true
      test-artifact-name: allure-results-seed-stand
      test-artifact-path: seed/build/allure-results
```

`working-directory` is the folder of this project, and `test-artifact-path` is relative to it. The upload fails
when the directory is missing, so add the workflow together with the first `*StandTest` class. The job reads the
stand settings like any other run, from the Owner configs, so non-secret defaults go in `src/main/resources`.
Without ci-kit, write the same job by hand: run `./gradlew :seed:standTest` and upload
`seed/build/allure-results`.

## 8. Adoption procedure

Run it to add the module to a project generated without it.

0. Check that the root build has what `seed/build.gradle` and `seed/gradle/dependencies.gradle` use, because they
   apply the plugins by id without a version and read the root catalog `libs`:
   - `build.gradle` applies `alias(libs.plugins.spotbugs)` and `alias(libs.plugins.archgate)`. Without the
     ArchGate plugin, run the adoption procedure of [architecture-verification.md](architecture-verification.md)
     first;
   - `gradle/libs.versions.toml` declares the libraries `testng`, `checkstyle` and `archgate-bom`;
   - `gradle/` has `compilation.gradle`, `code-analysis.gradle`, `tests.gradle` and `allure.gradle`, and
     `tools/` has the Checkstyle and SpotBugs configs.
1. Run `copier update --data with_seed_module=true`. It adds `seed/`, this spec, `SeedConfig` and
   `seed.properties`, but it does not change `settings.gradle`, which belongs to the project.
2. Append to `settings.gradle` (S1):

   ```groovy
   include 'seed'

   dependencyResolutionManagement {
       versionCatalogs {
           seedLibs {
               from(files('seed/gradle/seed.versions.toml'))
           }
       }
   }
   ```

3. If the project has local seed code (an extra `src/seed` source set, a `gradle/seed.gradle`), move each class
   into the package of section 2, delete the old source set and script, and replace its services, sessions and
   `System.getenv` calls with the main project's services, steps and configs (S3 to S6).
4. Run `./gradlew check` and check every box in section 9.

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] S1 to S12 hold, and S13 when the project has CI.
- [ ] `./gradlew check` passes, and its output lists `:seed:test` and `:seed:archgateCheck`.
- [ ] Two runs of `./gradlew :seed:run --args='generate --seed 1'` write identical files.
- [ ] `./gradlew :seed:standTest` runs only `*StandTest` classes.
